-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Photo is unique to this story (not used in any earlier package): Flickr photo 54954429093 by Ajay Suresh, CC BY 4.0, mirrored on Wikimedia Commons; license read from the Flickr page.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261109-brigham-nurses-strike', 'brigham-and-womens-nurses-set-open-ended-strike-nov-12', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'us', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Brigham and Women''s nurses set to begin open-ended strike Wednesday', 'More than 4,000 nurses could walk out at 7 a.m. Nov. 12 unless a deal is reached; talks resumed Monday with a federal mediator.', 'More than 4,000 nurses at Brigham and Women''s Hospital plan to walk off the job on Wednesday, Nov. 12, at 7 a.m. in an open-ended strike, their union, the Massachusetts Nurses Association (MNA), has said. Because the strike has no set end date, nurses would stay out until a contract deal is reached.

The two sides were scheduled to return to the bargaining table on Monday, Nov. 9, with a federal mediator, NBC Boston reported. The strike could still be called off if they reach an agreement before Wednesday morning.

## What the dispute is about

Union leaders have said staffing, rising health insurance costs and wages that keep pace with inflation are the main sticking points, Boston 25 News reported. The hospital, one of Mass General Brigham''s two flagship hospitals, has said its latest offer provides market-leading pay and competitive benefits, according to Healthcare IT News.

The nurses rejected the hospital''s "last, best and final" offer late last month and gave the required 10-day strike notice on Nov. 1, Boston.com reported. If it goes ahead, the walkout would be the largest nurses'' strike in Massachusetts history, WBUR reported.

## What to expect

Expect picket lines and news crews around the Brigham''s Longwood campus starting Wednesday. Patients with appointments or procedures should check with the hospital for the latest information.

Boston Daily will update this story as talks continue.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Brigham_and_Women%E2%80%99s_Hospital_%2854954429093%29.jpg/1280px-Brigham_and_Women%E2%80%99s_Hospital_%2854954429093%29.jpg', 'Brigham and Women''s Hospital in Boston''s Longwood Medical Area, November 2025 (file). Photo: Ajay Suresh via Flickr / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY 4.0', 'licensed', 'newsroom', 'chat:2026-11-09', 10, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-09T21:50:00.000Z', '2026-11-09T21:50:00.000Z');
